# --- build output ---
/target/
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Regenerated by `cargo build`; Tauri writes it from tauri.conf.json + capabilities.
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# --- editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- runtime state written by the app while testing ---
.eqforbeginner-beta/
# Pre-rename runs directory; kept so stale local dirs stay ignored.
.similarrew-beta/

# --- credentials and signing material (never commit) ---
.env
.env.*
*.p12
*.pem
*.cer
*.mobileprovision
*.keychain

# --- developer-local measurement data ---
# These are one person's room measurements and REW exports: hundreds of
# megabytes, personal, and not reproducible by anyone else. Everything the
# build and the test suite actually need is committed under assets/ and
# testdata/. Tests that want these fixtures skip with an explicit SKIPPED
# line when they are absent, so a fresh clone still runs green.
/measurments
/examples
/harnessexample
/debugfiles

# --- private working notes ---
# HANDOFF.md is the running session log between development sessions; it is
# process, not product. The public-facing state lives in README.md, STATUS.md
# and docs/.
HANDOFF.md
DEVELOPERINFO.md
howtobuild.txt
/.claude
CLAUDE.md

playground.txt